  <ferc:NotesToFinancialStatementsTextBlock id="HHFB845F6A13C048AB10E053139FD9FDD6" contextRef="HH6F430EA68AFC29D1DD829B0DDD45FFF4">&lt;div&gt;&lt;div&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-weight: bold;"&gt;STARTRANS IO, LLC&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-weight: bold;"&gt;NOTES TO FINANCIAL STATEMENTS&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-weight: bold;"&gt;FOR THE &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-weight: bold;"&gt;SIX&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-weight: bold;"&gt; MONTHS ENDED &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-weight: bold;"&gt;JUNE 30&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-weight: bold;"&gt;, 2026&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-weight: bold;"&gt;1. Regulatory Reporting and Presentation&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 5pt; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 5pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;The accompanying financial statements are prepared in accordance with the accounting requirements of the Federal Energy Regulatory Commission ("FERC"), as set forth in its applicable Uniform System of Accounts and published accounting releases and orders received by Startrans IO, LLC ("Startrans", "the Company", 'we", "our", or "us"), which is a comprehensive basis of accounting other than accounting principles generally accepted in the United States of America, ("GAAP"). The accompanying financial statements are prepared considering specific FERC reporting requirements and orders received by Startrans.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 5pt; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 5pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 5pt; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 5pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-weight: bold;"&gt;2. Business and Organization&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 5pt; margin-left: 13.5pt; margin-bottom: 5pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;Startrans IO, LLC ("Startrans", or the "Company") is a stand-alone transmission-only Delaware limited liability company formed in January 2008 to acquire an undivided interest in two jointly owned transmission lines and associated substations known as the Mead Facilities. The Mead Facilities are comprised of the Mead-Adelanto Project ("MAP"), a 1,296 MW, 500kV AC transmission line with substations extending 202 miles from southern Nevada to southern California, and the Mead-Phoenix Project ("MPP"), a 1,923 MW, 500kV AC transmission line with substations extending 256 miles from central Arizona to southern Nevada.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 5pt; margin-left: 15pt; margin-bottom: 5pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;In April 2008, the Company completed the acquisition of the undivided interests in the Mead Facilities, which was accounted for as an acquisition of assets and not as an acquisition of a continuing business. The Mead Facilities were acquired for a base purchase price of $39.5 million plus $479 thousand in transaction costs. The total purchase price paid for the Mead Facilities was funded by a combination of debt issued under senior secured term loan facilities ("Term Loan Facilities") (Note 5) and equity contributed by Startrans IH, LLC. With the purchase, Startrans applied for and became a Participating Transmission Owner ("PTO") within the California Independent System Operator Corporation ("CAISO") and executed a Transmission Control Agreement with CAISO and the other Mead Facilities transmission owners. CAISO is the Federal Energy Regulatory Commission's (the "FERC" or the "Commission") Regional Transmission Organization for the California region and, as such, CAISO bills and collects revenues from its load serving customers at FERC-approved rates. CAISO also maintains functional control over the Mead Facilities for certain transmission activities including scheduling and tariff administration and reviews plans concerning the expansion and upgrade of the facilities.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 5pt; margin-left: 13.5pt; margin-bottom: 5pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;The&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;Company is wholly owned by SIH, which is a wholly owned subsidiary of Startrans&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;I,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;Inc.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;Startrans I, Inc. is a wholly owned subsidiary of &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;Starmeads&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; I,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;LLC (formerly known as Startrans I, LLC).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;Starmeads&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; I,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;LLC is a wholly owned subsidiary of Meads Investment Holdings, LLC, an affiliate of the General Partner of Lotus Predecessor Fund I, LP (formerly known as Starwood Energy Infrastructure Fund, LP) and Lotus Predecessor Co-Invest Fund I, LP (formerly known as Starwood Energy Infrastructure Co-Invest Fund, LP).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-weight: bold;"&gt;3. Summary of Significant Accounting Policies &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 5pt; margin-bottom: 5pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-weight: bold;"&gt;Use of Estimates&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 5pt; margin-left: 15pt; margin-bottom: 5pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;The preparation of financial statements in conformity with accounting principles generally accepted in the United States of America ("US GAAP") requires management to make estimates and assumptions that affect the reported amounts of assets and liabilities and disclosure of contingent assets and liabilities as of the date of the financial statements and reported amounts of revenue and expenses during the reporting period. Actual results could differ from those estimates. Significant estimates and assumptions may &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;include, but&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; are not limited to the useful lives of long-lived assets, and the valuation of all derivative instruments (Note 7).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 5pt; margin-bottom: 5pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-weight: bold;"&gt;Regulatory Accounting&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 5pt; margin-left: 15pt; margin-bottom: 5pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;As a rate-regulated company, Startrans is subject to the regulatory jurisdiction of the FERC, which issues orders pertaining to rates, recovery of certain costs, including costs of transmission assets, condition of service, accounting, financing authorization, and operating related matters. The electric transmission operations of Startrans meet the US GAAP accounting standard that &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;recognizes the cost-based rate setting process, which results in differences in the application of USGAAP between regulated and nonregulated businesses. This ratemaking process results in the recording of regulatory assets or regulatory liabilities based on the probability of current and future estimated cash flows. Regulatory assets represent incurred or accrued costs that have been deferred because they are probable of future recovery from customers. Regulatory liabilities may represent collections from customers that have been deferred because they will be expended in the future or they may relate to the future cost of removal of assets. Startrans continuously reviews these regulatory assets to assess their ultimate recoverability within the approved regulatory guidelines. Startrans expects to fully recover these regulatory assets through its rates.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 5pt; margin-bottom: 5pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-weight: bold;"&gt;Cash and Cash Equivalents&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 5pt; margin-left: 15pt; margin-bottom: 5pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;Cash and cash equivalents include cash in banks and short-term investments. Short-term investments are comprised of highly liquid instruments with maturities of three months or less &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;at&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; the date of purchase. The Company maintains its cash and cash equivalents primarily on deposit with one financial institution and, at times, these balances exceed the federally insurable limit of $250 thousand. The Company believes it mitigates its risk by maintaining its cash and cash equivalents on deposit with a major financial institution.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 13.5pt; margin-bottom: 12pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;As of &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;June 30&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;, 2026, the Company had cash and cash equivalents balances in the following accounts:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 49.5pt; margin-bottom: 12pt; text-indent: 22.5pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;img style="-aw-left-pos: 0pt; -aw-rel-hpos: column; -aw-rel-vpos: paragraph; -aw-top-pos: 0pt; -aw-wrap-type: inline;" src="data:image/jpeg;base64," alt="" width="442" height="51" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 5pt; margin-left: 15pt; margin-bottom: 5pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;The commercial checking account is used to pay operations and maintenance ("O&amp;amp;M") expenses that have become due and payable.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 5pt; margin-left: 15pt; margin-bottom: 5pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 5pt; margin-bottom: 5pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-weight: bold;"&gt;Deferred Financing Costs&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 5pt; margin-left: 13.5pt; margin-bottom: 5pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;Deferred financing costs, consisting primarily of commitment fees, legal, and other direct costs incurred to obtain and restructure financing, are deferred and amortized over the expected financing term or over the estimated term of the loan. In 2025, the Company recorded $804 thousand as an asset for the commitment and legal fees associated with the debt attributable to the new Amended and Restated Credit Agreement with Associated Bank. An additional $2 thousand of these financing costs &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;was&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; incurred in 2026. These costs are being amortized using the effective interest method over the estimated term of the loan. For the &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;six&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; months &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;ended&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; June 30&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;, 2026, amortization expense of approximately $&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;8 &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;thousand was recorded in Amortization of Debt Disc and Expense within the statement of income.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 5pt; margin-bottom: 5pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-weight: bold;"&gt;Property, Plant and Equipment&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 5pt; margin-left: 15pt; margin-bottom: 5pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;Property, plant, and equipment is recorded at cost, based upon the purchase price paid in April 2008, and is being depreciated over an estimated group life of 48 years using the straight-line method. FERC reporting requirements prescribe that the historical accumulated depreciation associated with the assets be maintained and reported in the company general ledger system. The &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;48 year&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; estimated group life was based on, and is consistent with, the Arizona Public Service Company ("APS") depreciation rates.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;APS is the only other regulated entity which &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;owns&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; an interest in the Mead facilities. Depreciation expense was $&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;228&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; thousand for the &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;six&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; months ended&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; June 30&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;, 2026.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;All new property and equipment &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;is&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; being depreciated on a straight-line basis over the estimated useful lives of the respective assets. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;At&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;June 30&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;, 2026, transmission plant accumulated depreciation and amortization amounted to $15.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;8&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; million.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 5pt; margin-left: 15pt; margin-bottom: 5pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;The Company evaluates its long-lived assets for impairment as events or changes in circumstances indicate the carrying value of these assets may not be fully recoverable. If the undiscounted future cash flows before interest associated with the expected uses and eventual disposition of those assets are not greater than the carrying value of those assets, the Company &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;would&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; record an impairment loss based on the fair value of the asset.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;There was no impairment of long-lived assets for the &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;six&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; months ended &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;June 30&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;, 2026.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 5pt; margin-bottom: 5pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-weight: bold;"&gt;Revenue Recognition&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 5pt; margin-left: 15pt; margin-bottom: 5pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;The Company records revenue proportionally throughout the year based on its current Transmission Revenue Requirement ("TRR"), which provides for a fixed amount of revenue per year irrespective of usage. CAISO bills load-serving customers for actual usage based on the TRR and estimated load. Differences between the billed rates and TRR are recorded to the Transmission Revenue Balancing Account ("TRBA") (Note 4).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 5pt; margin-bottom: 5pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-weight: bold;"&gt;Income Taxes&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 5pt; margin-left: 15pt; margin-bottom: 5pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;The Company accounts for income taxes using &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;the accrual&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; method. This practice requires the recognition of deferred tax assets and liabilities for the expected future tax consequences attributable to differences between the financial statement carrying amounts of existing assets and liabilities and their respective tax bases. Deferred tax assets, representing future tax benefits, are recognized to the extent that their realization is more likely than not to occur. Valuation allowances are established when necessary to reduce deferred tax assets to the amount that is more likely than not to be realized.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 5pt; margin-left: 15pt; margin-bottom: 5pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;The Company considers the future taxable income and ongoing tax planning strategies in assessing the need for a valuation allowance. The deferred tax provision or benefit represents the change in the deferred tax assets and liabilities from the prior year. Deferred taxes presented in these statements are prepared on a separate return basis as the Company is a single &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;member&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; LLC.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 5pt; margin-bottom: 5pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-weight: bold;"&gt;Recently Issued Accounting Pronouncements&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 5pt; margin-left: 13.5pt; margin-bottom: 5pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;ASU2023-09 &amp;#8211; Income Taxes: Improvements to Income Tax Disclosures. In December 2023, a new accounting standard was issued that expands disclosures relating to income taxes. The expanded disclosures include a tabular income tax rate reconciliation, disclosure of specific reconciliation categories and reconciling items, the amount of income taxes paid by jurisdictions, and other disclosures. The adoption of the new standard will not &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;impact&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; our accounting for income taxes or our financial statement results. On July 4, 2025, tax legislation commonly referred to as the &amp;#8220;One Big Beautiful Bill Act (OB3&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;or OBBBA)&amp;#8221; was enacted into law. As the Company's operations are rate-regulated, major components of the legislation, such as bonus depreciation and changes to the deductibility of business interest expense, do not apply.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; As such, the overall impact of OB3 did not have a material effect on the Company's financial statements.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; page-break-after: avoid; line-height: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-size: 12pt; font-weight: bold;"&gt;Going Concern &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; page-break-after: avoid; line-height: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-size: 12pt; font-weight: bold;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 13.5pt; margin-bottom: 12pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;The Company does not believe that any &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;condition&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-size: 12pt;"&gt; or events exist that raise substantial doubt about the entity&amp;#8217;s ability to continue as a going concern for the &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;6&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;-month period the financial statements were available to be issued.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; page-break-after: avoid; line-height: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-size: 12pt; font-weight: bold;"&gt;Concentration of Credit Risk&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; page-break-after: avoid; line-height: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-size: 12pt; font-weight: bold;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 13.5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;Certain financial instruments potentially subject the Company to &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;concentrations&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;of&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; credit risk.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;These&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;financial&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;instruments consist&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;primarily of&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;cash and&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;cash&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;equivalents with one&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;financial institution in an account, which &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;exceed&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; FDIC limits. The Company recognizes a concentration risk due to its exclusive reliance on sales to the California Independent System Operator (CAISO), which accounts for 100% of the Company's revenue and Accounts Receivable. However, given CAISO's role as a central operator of the high-voltage power grid and its established position within California's energy market, the risk associated with this concentration is mitigated by CAISO's stable and critical operational nature. While any changes in CAISO's purchasing policies, financial health, or regulatory environment could potentially impact the Company's financial position, results of operations, and cash flows, the essential services provided by CAISO and its regulatory oversight reduce the likelihood of significant adverse effects.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 13.5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 13.5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-weight: bold;"&gt;4. Regulatory Matters&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 13.5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-indent: 13.5pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-weight: bold;"&gt;Rate Case&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-indent: 13.5pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-weight: bold;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 13.5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;On October 30, 2020, Startrans filed a new TRR rate case in Docket No. ER21-263. In an order issued December 30, 2020, the FERC accepted the Startrans proposed TRR, suspended it for a nominal period, to be effective January 1, 2021, subject to refund, and set the matter for hearing and settlement procedures. Additionally, the FERC instituted a section 206 investigation with respect to the reasonableness of the proposed TRR. Settlement discussions were held with the parties to the proceeding and on June 2, &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;2021&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; Startrans submitted to FERC an Offer of Settlement (Settlement) which resolved all issues to all participants in the ER21-263 proceeding. Specifically, the Settlement established a new base TRR of $2,950 thousand, a reduction of $350 thousand from the &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;filed&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;-for level of $3,300 thousand. On June 11, 2021, the FERC Chief Judge approved an order that granted a motion that authorized the interim implementation of the settlement TRR effective on July 1, &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;2021&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; and, on August 6, 2021, the Settlement Judge certified the uncontested Settlement to the Commission for its approval. On October 21, 2021, the Commission approved the Settlement by Letter Order. The Settlement further requires Startrans to file a revised TRR no later than November 1, 2025, and request an effective date no later than January 1, 2026.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 13.5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;In accordance with the terms of the Settlement, Startrans coordinated with the CAISO to provide refunds, with interest at the FERC interest rate, for the difference between the amounts received based on the filed-for TRR ($3,300 thousand) and the TRR set forth in the Settlement ($2,950 thousand). Refunds were required to be made back to the January 8, &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;2021&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; refund effective date. The actual refund obligation was determined by &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;the CAISO&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;. The refunds were made pursuant &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;to the CAISO payment &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;schedule&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; and such refunds were completed in July 2022. On August 29, 2022, the Company filed a refund report with the FERC.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 13.5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 13.5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;In accordance with the terms of its TRR rate case Settlement in Docket No. ER21-263, approved by the FERC in a Letter Order dated October 21, 2021, Startrans filed a new TRR rate case in Docket No. ER26-302 on October 29, 2025. In this filing, the Company proposed to reflect a rate increase of $906 thousand to its base TRR, resulting in a proposed TRR of $3,856 thousand, to become effective January 1, 2026. In an order issued December 31, 2025, the FERC accepted the Startrans proposed TRR, suspended it for five months, to be effective June 1, 2026, subject to refund, and set the matter for hearing and settlement procedures. Additionally, the FERC instituted a section 205 investigation with respect to the reasonableness of the proposed TRR. An initial settlement conference was held with the parties to the proceeding on February 19, &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;2026&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; and &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;an &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;additional settlement conference &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;is scheduled for September 2, 20&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;26&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;During this time&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;, responses&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; to data&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; requests have been &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;provided.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 13.5pt; margin-bottom: 11pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 15pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-weight: bold;"&gt;Transmission Revenue Balancing Account&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 5pt; margin-left: 15pt; margin-bottom: 5pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;The CAISO tariff provides for a true-up mechanism in which the CAISO calculates any over-collection or under-collection of transmission revenues to the authorized revenue requirement and either credits or charges that difference to transmission customers in the subsequent year. In addition, any wheeling revenues and usage revenues received are included in the calculation and effectively refunded to the transmission customer over the subsequent year. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;At&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;June 30&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;, 2026, the Transmission Revenue Balancing Account balance was approximately $&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;132&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; thousand under-collected. On the balance sheet, this amount is included in Miscellaneous Current and Accrued Assets.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 13.5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 13.5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 13.5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-weight: bold;"&gt;Regulatory Assets&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 5pt; margin-left: 13.5pt; margin-bottom: 5pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;The Company recorded a regulatory asset of $341 thousand as of December 31, 2025, and an additional $&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;174 &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;thousand in the &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;six &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;months ended &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;June 30&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;, 2026, related to the costs to prepare and file its Transmission Owners Tariff in its new rate case in ER26-302, filed with the FERC in October 2025. These capitalized costs are presented on the balance sheets as part of Other Regulatory Assets.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 5pt; margin-left: 13.5pt; margin-bottom: 5pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;As of &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;June 30&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;, 2026, $&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;3&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;8 thousand is presented on the balance sheets as Other Regulatory Assets, related to the change in valuation of the Startrans interest rate swap (Note 6). Startrans &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;is able to&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; recover amounts paid to the interest rate swap counterparty under the terms of the Company transmission tariff.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 13.5pt; margin-bottom: 12pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-size: 12pt; font-weight: bold;"&gt;Regulatory Liabilities&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 5pt; margin-left: 13.5pt; margin-bottom: 5pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;In 2018, the Company initially accounted for the change in the federal corporate tax rate from 34% to 21% caused by the Tax Cuts and Jobs Act, by recording an income tax benefit. However, as a result of guidance provided by the Commission in its orders issued November 21, &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;2019&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; in Order No. 864 and April 16, &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;2020&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; in Order No. 864-A, which spoke to the Commission's requirement for public utilities with transmission stated rates to address excess accumulated deferred income taxes resulting from the Tax Cuts and Job Act in their next rate case, the &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;Company reversed a portion of the income tax benefit previously recorded. Correspondingly, the Company recorded a regulatory liability in Other Regulatory Liabilities - Account 254.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;For the &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;six&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; months ended&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; June 30&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;, 2026, approximately $(0.0&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;24&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;) &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;thousand&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; of the excess accumulated deferred income taxes was amortized and recorded in the statements of income. As a result, the regulatory liability in Other Regulatory Liabilities - Account 254 amounted to $562 thousand &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;at&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; June 30&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;, 2026.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 5pt; margin-left: 13.5pt; margin-bottom: 5pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;The Company also recorded a regulatory liability of $&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;38&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; thousand related to the change in valuation of the Startrans interest rate swap (Note 6), in Derivative Instrument Liabilities on the balance sheets.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 5pt; margin-bottom: 5pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-weight: bold;"&gt;5. Debt Obligations&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 13.5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;On April 22, &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;2008&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; the Company entered into a Credit Agreement with Erste &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;Abwicklungsanstalt&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; ('EAA"), (formerly &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;Portigon&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; AG and, prior to &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;Portigon&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; AG, formerly &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;WestLB&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; AG), as the Lender and Administrative Agent and closed on secured bank financing, consisting of an aggregate amount of up to $9.7 million in senior secured term loan facilities (the "Term Loan Facilities") in accordance with the terms of the Credit Agreement. The $9.7 million consisted of (&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;i&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;) a $7.6 million Term Loan, (ii) a $1.6 million Delayed Draw #1 Loan, and (iii) a $0.5 million Delayed Draw #2 Loan. The $7.6 million Term Loan matured on the seventeen (17) year anniversary of the closing date and required quarterly payments of principal and interest. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;On June 26, 2012, the Company made prepayments on the remaining outstanding principal balances on the Delayed Draw #1 Loan and the Delayed Draw #2 Loan, thereby extinguishing these two term loans. On March&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;31, &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;2025&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; and June 27, 2025, the&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;Company and EAA executed amendments to the Credit Agreement to extend the Term Loan Maturity Date to June&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;30, &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;2025&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; and July 31, 2025, respectively. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 13.5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 13.5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;On July 31, 2025, Erste &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;Abwicklungsanstalt&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; assigned the Company&amp;#8217;s existing term loan to Associated Bank, N.A. (&amp;#8220;Associated Bank&amp;#8221;) and Associated Bank became the sole lender and administrative agent under the previously existing credit agreement. On July 31, 2025, the Company entered into an Amended and Restated Credit Agreement (the &amp;#8220;Amended and Restated Credit Agreement&amp;#8221;) with Associated Bank, as the Lender and Administrative Agent and refinanced its existing $2.31 million term loan and added an additional $2.0 million term loan to rebalance the Company&amp;#8217;s capital structure, resulting in a $4.31 million senior secured term loan (the &amp;#8220;Term Loan&amp;#8221;). The Amended and Restated Credit Agreement extended the maturity date for the Term Loan to July 31, 2030, and requires quarterly payments of principal and interest as set forth in a new amortization schedule. In connection with the Amended and Restated Credit Agreement, the previously required debt ratio covenants and exit fee were removed; however, certain minimum debt ratios are required for distributions from the Company. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 13.5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 13.5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;As discussed in note 1, the&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;Company is a wholly owned subsidiary of Startrans IH,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;LLC (the &amp;#8220;Parent&amp;#8221;, and collectively with the&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;Company, the &amp;#8220;Startrans Entities&amp;#8221;).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;The Parent also had a Credit Agreement with Associated Bank (Associated Bank and the Startrans Entities are further referred to as the &amp;#8220;Parties&amp;#8221;). The Parent also entered into an Amended and Restated Credit Agreement with Associated Bank.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 7.5pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 15pt; margin-bottom: 7.5pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;As of &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;June 30&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;, 2026, the balances outstanding under the Credit Agreement were:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 5pt; margin-bottom: 5pt; text-align: center; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;img style="-aw-left-pos: 0pt; -aw-rel-hpos: column; -aw-rel-vpos: paragraph; -aw-top-pos: 0pt; -aw-wrap-type: inline;" src="data:image/jpeg;base64," alt="" width="472" height="138" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 27pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 22.5pt; margin-bottom: 12pt; text-align: justify; page-break-inside: avoid; page-break-after: avoid; line-height: 12pt; widows: 0; orphans: 0;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;Scheduled minimum annual principal payments due under terms of the Amended and Restated Credit Agreement are as follows:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 5pt; margin-left: 58.5pt; margin-bottom: 5pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;img style="display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;" src="data:image/jpeg;base64," alt="" width="520" height="165" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 7.5pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;The debt is collateralized by &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;all of&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; the Company&amp;#8217;s assets, including its transmission assets, and has a variable interest rate based on Adjusted Daily Compounded SOFR plus 2.75%. On August 7, 2025, the Company entered an interest rate swap transaction with Associated Bank on the $4.31 million Term Loan, converting the variable rate debt to fixed rate debt (See Note 6). &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-weight: bold;"&gt;6. Derivative Instruments&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-indent: 1.5pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 13.5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;The Company uses variable rate debt to finance its operations. The debt obligations expose the Company to variability in interest payments due to changes in interest rates. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;In order to&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; reduce the variability in interest payments, the Company has entered into an interest rate swap agreement to limit the fluctuations in cash &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;flows&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; resulting from interest rate risk. These swaps effectively change the variable-rate cash flow exposure on the debt obligations to fixed cash flows. Under &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;terms of the&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; interest rate swap, the Company receives variable interest rate payments and makes fixed interest payments, thereby creating the equivalent of fixed rate debt for the notional amount, as listed below:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 5pt; margin-bottom: 5pt; text-align: center; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;img style="-aw-left-pos: 0pt; -aw-rel-hpos: column; -aw-rel-vpos: paragraph; -aw-top-pos: 0pt; -aw-wrap-type: inline;" src="data:image/jpeg;base64," alt="" width="442" height="69" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 13.5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;The Company accounts for this interest rate swap in accordance with the authoritative guidance for derivative instruments. The Company has not &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;elected&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; hedge accounting treatment. As the Company &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;is able to&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; recover cash flows associated with the interest rate swap under its TRR, changes in the fair value of the interest rate swap are reflected in the corresponding regulatory asset or liability account during the applicable period.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 5pt; margin-left: 15pt; margin-bottom: 5pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;The Company does not &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;enter into&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; derivative instruments for any purpose other than cash flow hedging and does not make speculative investments using derivative instruments. By using derivative financial instruments to hedge its exposure to changes in interest rates, Startrans exposes itself to counter-party credit risk and market risk. The Company believes it minimizes the credit risk by &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;entering into&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; transactions with a &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;counter-party&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; with investment grade credit ratings. If the &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;counter-party&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; was unable to meet its obligations under the interest rate swap, the Company would be exposed to variable interest rate risk.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 5pt; margin-left: 15pt; margin-bottom: 5pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;Market risk is the positive or negative effect on the value of a derivative instrument that results from a change in interest rates. The market risk associated with interest rate contracts is managed by establishing and monitoring parameters that limit the types and degree of market risk that may be undertaken.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 5pt; margin-left: 15pt; margin-bottom: 5pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;The location and amounts of derivative fair values in the balance sheet for the &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;six&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; months &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;ended&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;June 30&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;, 2026, are:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 5pt; margin-bottom: 5pt; text-align: center; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;img style="-aw-left-pos: 0pt; -aw-rel-hpos: column; -aw-rel-vpos: paragraph; -aw-top-pos: 0pt; -aw-wrap-type: inline;" src="data:image/jpeg;base64," alt="" width="601" height="157" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 5pt; margin-left: 13.5pt; margin-bottom: 5pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;The effect of derivative instruments on income for the &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;six &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;months &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;ended&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; June 30&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;, &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;2026&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; is:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 5pt; margin-left: 15pt; margin-bottom: 5pt; text-align: center; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;img style="-aw-left-pos: 0pt; -aw-rel-hpos: column; -aw-rel-vpos: paragraph; -aw-top-pos: 0pt; -aw-wrap-type: inline;" src="data:image/jpeg;base64," alt="" width="588" height="148" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 5pt; margin-bottom: 5pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-weight: bold;"&gt;7. Fair Value of Financial Instruments&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 5pt; margin-left: 15pt; margin-bottom: 5pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;Fair value is defined as the price that would be received to sell an asset or paid to transfer a liability in an orderly transaction between market participants at the measurement date in a principal or most advantageous market. Fair value is a market-based measurement that is determined based on inputs, which refer broadly to assumptions that market participant's use in pricing assets or liabilities. These inputs can be readily observable, market corroborated, or generally unobservable firm inputs. The Company often makes certain assumptions that market participants would use in pricing the asset or liability, including assumptions about risk, and the risks inherent in the inputs to valuation techniques. The Company uses valuation techniques that maximize the use of observable inputs and minimize the use of unobservable inputs.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 5pt; margin-left: 15pt; margin-bottom: 5pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;The Company considers the impact of nonperformance risk (including credit risk) from a market participant perspective in the measurement of the fair value of assets and liabilities. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;At&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; December 31, 2025, the Company determined that nonperformance risk would have no material &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;impact on their financial position or results of operations. To assess nonperformance risk, the Company considered information such as collateral requirements, netting arrangements and letters of credit guarantees.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 5pt; margin-left: 15pt; margin-bottom: 5pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;The established fair value hierarchy prioritizes the inputs to valuation techniques used to measure fair value in three broad levels. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;The fair&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; value guidance requires that assets and liabilities be classified in their entirety based on the level of input that is significant to the fair value measurement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 5pt; margin-left: 15pt; margin-bottom: 5pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;Assessing the significance of a particular input may require judgment considering factors specific to the asset or &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;liability, and&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; may affect the valuation of the asset or liability and their placement within the fair value hierarchy. The Company classifies fair value balances based on the fair value hierarchy defined as follows:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 5pt; margin-bottom: 5pt; text-align: right; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 5pt; margin-left: 79.5pt; margin-bottom: 5pt; text-indent: -57.6pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;Level 1 Quoted prices are available in active markets for identical assets and liabilities as of the reporting date. Active markets are those in which transactions for the asset or liability occur in sufficient frequency and volume to provide pricing information on an ongoing basis.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 5pt; margin-left: 79.5pt; margin-bottom: 5pt; text-indent: -57.6pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;Level 2 Pricing inputs are not quoted prices but are either directly or indirectly observable as of the reporting date, including those financial instruments that are valued using models or other valuation methodologies. These models are primarily industry standard models that consider various assumptions, including quoted forward prices for commodities, time value, volatility factors, and current market and contractual prices for the underlying instruments, as well as other relevant economic measures. Substantially &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;all of&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; these assumptions are observable in the marketplace throughout the full term of the instrument, which can be derived from observable data or are supported by observable levels at which transactions are executed in the marketplace.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 5pt; margin-left: 79.5pt; margin-bottom: 5pt; text-indent: -57.6pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;Level 3 Pricing inputs include significant inputs that are generally less observable from objective sources. These inputs may be used with &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;internally-developed&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; methodologies that result in management's best estimate of fair value. Level 3 instruments include those that may be more structured or otherwise tailored to customers' needs. At each balance sheet date, the Company performs an analysis of all instruments subject to fair value measurement and includes in Level 3 &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;all of&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; those whose fair value is based on significant unobservable inputs.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 5pt; margin-left: 15pt; margin-bottom: 5pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;The Company measures &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;it&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; financial instruments at fair value. The following tables present the fair value and hierarchy levels for the financial instruments as of &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;June 30&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;, 2026: &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 22.5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;img style="display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;" src="data:image/jpeg;base64," alt="" width="575" height="264" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 5pt; margin-left: 15pt; margin-bottom: 5pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;The fair value of the interest rate derivative is based on quoted prices for similar instruments from a commercial bank.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 5pt; margin-left: 15pt; margin-bottom: 5pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-weight: bold;"&gt;8. Income Taxes&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 5pt; margin-left: 13.5pt; margin-bottom: 5pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;For the &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;six&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; months &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;ended&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;June 30&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;, 2026, the Company had a current tax provision of &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;$&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;thousand, and&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; recorded a deferred tax expense of $&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;69&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; thousand.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;The deferred tax provision is comprised of deferred federal and state income taxes of $&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;47 &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;thousand and $&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;22 &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;thousand, respectively, for the &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;six&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; months ended&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; June 30&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;, 2026. Partially offsetting the deferred tax provision, is a deferred tax benefit of $(0.0&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;24&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;) thousand, which is attributable to the amortization of the excess accumulated deferred taxes ("Excess ADIT") which the Company previously recorded in December 2020. In accordance with FERC Order 864, as supplemented by FERC Order 864-A, the Company recorded the Excess ADIT in order to create a regulatory liability (FERC account 254) that results from the change in the federal tax rate under the Tax Cuts and Job Acts, which was effective for the year beginning January1, 2018. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 5pt; margin-left: 13.5pt; margin-bottom: 5pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;The reconciliation between the statutory tax rate and the effective tax rate is due to state income taxes, changes in valuation allowances and the establishment of the Excess ADIT. As of&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; June&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; 3&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;, 2026, there are no uncertain tax positions recorded by the Company. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 5pt; margin-left: 13.5pt; margin-bottom: 5pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;The tax effect of temporary differences, which gave rise to the deferred tax assets and liabilities, is as follows:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 5pt; margin-left: 13.5pt; margin-bottom: 5pt; text-align: center; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;img style="-aw-left-pos: 0pt; -aw-rel-hpos: column; -aw-rel-vpos: paragraph; -aw-top-pos: 0pt; -aw-wrap-type: inline;" src="data:image/jpeg;base64," alt="" width="592" height="256" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 5pt; margin-left: 13.5pt; margin-bottom: 5pt; text-align: center; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-weight: bold; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-weight: bold;"&gt;9. Related Party Transactions&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 5pt; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;In September 2008, the Company entered into a Management Services Agreement with Startrans IH, LLC, an affiliate of Startrans. This agreement calls for Startrans to pay Startrans IH, LLC an annual fee of approximately $120 thousand plus personnel and &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;third party&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; cost for management services provided under the agreement. The Management Services Agreement covers all prior and future services provided by Startrans IH, &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;LLC&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; to Startrans. The fee is adjusted each year based on changes to the Producer Price Index. For the &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;six&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; months ended &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;June 30&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;, 2026, the Company incurred total costs of $&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;426&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; thousand under the Management Services Agreement &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;of &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;which&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; $112 thousand&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; was unpaid and included in Miscellaneous Current and Accrued Liabilities on the balance sheets.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="width: 381pt; display: inline-block; -aw-tabstop-align: left; -aw-tabstop-pos: 381pt;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-weight: bold;"&gt;10. Commitments and Contingencies&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 5pt; margin-left: 15pt; margin-bottom: 5pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;The Company is subject to contingencies as part of its normal business operations. Legal expenses related to such matters are &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;expensed&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; as incurred. Management does not believe that any contingencies will have a material adverse effect on the Company's financial position or results of operations.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 12pt; margin-bottom: 12pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 12pt; margin-bottom: 12pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:NotesToFinancialStatementsTextBlock>
